#
# Refuses a push that would not pass the gates that answer inside a minute:
# the quick ones, the suite, the fuzz sweep, and the Composer-free autoloader.
#
# The coverage floor is deliberately not here. Git opens the connection to the
# remote BEFORE running this hook, because it has to tell the hook what would
# be pushed — so everything this takes is time an idle connection waits. The
# first version ran the whole of `composer check`, and five minutes of
# coverage shards later the server had given up: "Connection to github.com
# closed by remote host", and the push failed after every gate had passed. A
# hook that can make a good push fail is worse than one that checks less.
#
# So `composer check` keeps the floor, CI always runs it, and a coverage
# regression is the one thing these hooks leave to CI.
#
# Three things no single machine can try, and the run says so when it passes:
# the suite on the other PHP versions, the library on whichever side of `intl`
# this machine is not on, and Litmus against the example server.
#
# Installed with `composer hooks`. Bypassed with `git push --no-verify`.

exec composer gates:push
